# Day 1: Data Loading & Power Query Basics

## Topics Practiced

- Importing data into Power BI using Text/CSV
- Opening Power Query Editor
- Checking column names
- Checking and changing data types
- Renaming columns
- Removing unnecessary columns
- Removing duplicate rows
- Checking for blank/null values
- Applying transformations using Close & Apply

## Power BI Workflow

Get Data → Transform Data → Power Query → Clean/Transform Data → Close & Apply

## What I Learned

Power Query is used in Power BI to clean and transform data before
loading it into the data model.

I practiced basic data preparation tasks such as changing data types,
renaming columns, removing unnecessary columns, removing duplicates,
and checking missing values.

## Tools Used

- Power BI Desktop
- Power Query
